ethan: FYI I'm hitting sporadic "Unexpected end of JSON input" in the Node SDK when consuming SSE streams. Repro in sample-app (node 18 + sdk-js 0.6.3). Seems to happen when the client tab is closed mid-flight or when our auth refresh/reconnect happens. Anyone seen this?

maya: python saw the same class of bug earlier but masked by our readline/iter logic. Node code currently assumes each 'data:' event arrives whole in a single 'data' callback which is not true across networks/proxies.

vikas: can you share a tiny repro and the stack trace? I want to add a test. /cc @tori for what runtime does on token refresh.

ethan: repro snippet:
```js
const res = await fetch(url, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${TOKEN}` } });
const reader = res.body.getReader();
let buf = '';
while (true) {
  const { value, done } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  buf += new TextDecoder().decode(value);
  const parts = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = parts.pop(); // keep trailing partial
  for (const p of parts) {
    if (!p) continue;
    if (p.startsWith('data: ')) {
      const payload = JSON.parse(p.slice(6)); // throws on partial JSON
      handle(payload);
    }
  }
}
```
stack: `SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at JSON.parse (sdk/index.js:88)`

tori: runtime behavior: when token rotation occurs we tear down the SSE socket and open a fresh one. We don't currently emit any resume metadata, so any partial event in-flight is lost unless the client keeps that trailing bytes across the reconnect.

maya: also note chunk ordering can be non-atomic — reverse proxies and TCP segmentation can split a single SSE event across multiple chunks. Clients should treat SSE as an unstructured byte stream and reassemble events before parsing.

vikas: action: file bug and patch node SDK to maintain a persistent tail buffer across reconnects and only call JSON.parse once we detect the '\n\n' delimiter. Also add unit tests that simulate aborted sockets, delayed chunk delivery, and auth rotate. Will add a telemetry counter `sse_parse_error`.

ci-bot: Created issue #4412: "sdk-js(node): SSE partial-chunk parse error on reconnect/auth-rotate - add tail buffer & tests" assigned to vikas.

jen: small interim workaround for sample apps/docs: recommend increasing token TTL for long streams or proactively refreshing before starting long streams. Also publish a robust parsing snippet showing persistent buffer and safe JSON.parse with try/catch and requeue on error.

ethan: will update sample-app README and onboarding guide with the workaround and a note recommending server-side sequence numbers. If runtime can include a seq on each event we can detect gaps.

tori: runtime can add an optional control event before planned rotates: `event: control\ndata: {"type":"pre_rotate","last_seq": 1024}\n\n` and on new stream echo `event: control\ndata: {"type":"resume","last_seq":1024}\n\n` so clients can reconcile. For forced 401s we'll try to emit resume metadata on the new stream. I'll open a PR.

vikas: plan: 1) sticky tail buffer + tests, 2) optional strict seq-checking when server provides seqs, 3) telemetry + alert, 4) update sample-app. ETA: patch + tests tomorrow.

ci-bot: Issue #4412 tagged ["devex","sdk-node","sse","high-priority"], linked runtime issue #4413.

ethan: thanks 00b; follow-ups: vikas (sdk patch + tests + telem), tori (runtime pre-rotate/resume PR), me (docs + sample-app). I'll smoke-test once PRs land. :thumbsup:
